# Source: https://github.com/colorcube/Linux-on-Honor-Magicbook-14-Pro/issues/3 (nikube, 2026-08-03)
#
# HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P): the Goodix touchpad (GXT7863, 27C6:01E0) exposes two
# vendor HID collections (usage pages FF00/FF01) that Windows leaves unbound. Linux maps
# them into a third input device "GXT7863:00 27C6:01E0 UNKNOWN", which emits a
# KEY_BRIGHTNESSUP/DOWN press without a release. The kernel then autorepeats it at
# ~30 Hz and the screen jumps between dark and full brightness.
# Mapping the vendor usages to "reserved" stops the ghost keys inside the kernel, for
# every desktop. 0xff010001 (micmute) has the same stuck-press bug: after resume it can
# toggle the microphone at autorepeat rate until another key is pressed. The real
# mic-mute key (F7) arrives via huawei-wmi, so this usage is not needed (colorcube,
# verified on BIOS 1.13 with libinput debug-events).
# Earlier analysis: jean bzh (Fedora forum), sujoshua, Osama-A-Abbas.
evdev:input:b0018v27C6p01E0*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_ff010003=reserved
 KEYBOARD_KEY_ff010004=reserved
 KEYBOARD_KEY_ff010001=reserved
